<<<
is not to aim the same as to design? is not to claim to represent? does not oblivious mean insensible? is not to doubt to be unconvinced?
===
is not to *aim* the same as to *design*? is not to *claim* to *represent*? does not *oblivious* mean *insensible*? is not to *doubt* to *be unconvinced*?
>>>

<<<
would not so that convey the same as in order that? is not regarding considering? is not -ly the adverbial ending, & is not won to be modified by an adverb?
===
would not *so that* convey the same as *in order that*? is not *regard*ing *consider*ing? is not -ly the adverbial ending, & is not *won* to be modified by an adverb?
>>>

<<<
&, if in view of is English, why should with a view of be unEnglish?
===
&, if *in view of* is English, why should *with a view of* be unEnglish?
>>>

